# Split from server.lang - dialogue bundle (aetherhaven_dialogue_blacksmith)
# Full translation keys are aetherhaven.dialogue.blacksmith.<lineKey> (see Hytale I18nModule).
aetherhaven.dialogue.blacksmith.repairGear=Fix my gear (pay in gold coins)
aetherhaven.dialogue.blacksmith.openGeodes=Crack open geodes (5 gold each)
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_abandoned.body=There are no hard feelings. If you decide you need precision metalwork again, just ask me directly.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_abandoned.c0=Understood.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_abandoned.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_building.body=Once the shop structure is fully complete, I will move in and calibrate the weapon bench. Please return to that location so we can finalize the setup together.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_building.c0=I need to cancel this quest for now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_building.c1=I will continue working on it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_building.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_done.body=The bench is solid and level. Now I can control the heat precisely. We are done shipping ore across the map; we use only the local ground here to ensure material consistency.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_done.c0=Hammer well.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_done.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_accepted.body=When the house construction is finished, register my name on the bookshelf inside and come find me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_accepted.c0=I will let you know when it is done.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_accepted.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_finish.body=Finally. A roof that does not smell like someone else's cooking.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_finish.c0=Enjoy your new home.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_finish.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_offer.body=My current workspace gives me blisters and ruins the temper on my tools. I need a permanent roof over my head. Stake the same type of house plot as anyone else and register me once the walls are solid.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_offer.c0=I will stake a house for you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_offer.c1=Not right now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_offer.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_remind.body=Metal cannot be rushed, and neither should your building progress. Register me on the bookshelf once the house is complete, then come speak to me in person to close the loop.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_remind.c0=I understand. I will handle it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_house_remind.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_quest_shop.body=Corin's inn is fine for sleeping but terrible for swinging a hammer. I require a proper shop with walls, a counter, and a weapon bench of my own. Take this token, stake the plot with your staff, and pay the materials listed on the sign. When it stands, meet me at the bench so we can close the order.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_quest_shop.c0=We will get it built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_quest_shop.c1=Not right now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_quest_shop.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_shop_accepted.body=Good. I will camp at the inn until the chimney aligns correctly and the draft is stable. Then meet me at the bench so we can seal the agreement and begin work.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_shop_accepted.c0=See you there.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.garren_shop_accepted.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.rep_reward_25.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.rep_reward_50.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.body=Garren Vale. The wind is calm enough for the forge to behave consistently. Metal out here has specific properties, and I am here to understand them rather than argue with them.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c2=You wanted to talk about a house.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c3=The house is finished and your name is on the registry.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c4=The house is still being constructed.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c5=It is good to see you handling steel with care.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c6=The shop is built. The bench is level and ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c7=About the forge build...
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c8=You said you needed a functional forge here.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.c9=Watch your fingers near the anvil.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.root.speaker=Garren Vale
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.love=Excellent! I will not forget the quality of this gift.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.like=Solid structure. I will add this to the premium bin immediately.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.neutral=Acceptable. I will store it for future reference if needed.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.dislike=I appreciate the intent, but my forge requires specific ore grades, not... this.

aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.fallback=Speak plainly. I am very busy.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.0=The forge is silent enough that I can hear a hinge settle perfectly. That is a very good sign.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.1=Wipe the mud off your boots immediately. Ash on the tempering table ruins the finish on everything I touch.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.2=I am between jobs, so I have a moment to talk. How can I help you?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.3=I should do something with the slack tub... oh! I didn't see you there. What's on your mind?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.4=Need a reading on an ingot? Place it on the bench. I will check the hardness and resonance.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.5=The shop smells of coal and precision. I prefer it exactly that way.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.6=I filed a burr off the tongs earlier. Small work, but it prevents burns later.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.7=Most people come here for steel, not a chat. But it's a good day, so either works for me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.8=If you have a new repair order, I'll add it to my queue.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.greeting.9=Tell me what you need before I glove up. Once I start heating the metal, I avoid distractions.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.love.0=I'm always on the lookout for high-grade stock.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.love.1=Rare ore placed on this bench gets treated with immediate priority.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.love.2=Fine armor pieces tell me you understand survival in these lands.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.love.3=Geodes are a calculated risk I enjoy. Feel free to donate a few if you don't care to know what's inside.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.love.4=Clean plate or a tight coil cable shows that you value craft over clutter.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.dislike.0=I do not need raw cobble pretending to be useful material.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.dislike.1=Bone trophies belong on a hunter's wall, not in my workshop.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.dislike.2=If it turns to grit under pressure, keep it out of my shop.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.dislike.3=Cheap trinkets with no temper or edge waste both our time.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.main_hub.hint.dislike.4=Rotten wood and soggy fiber make poor fuel. Stick to coal.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.birthday.greeting=My birthday and you stopped by the forge. That means plenty.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.love.birthday=It is my birthday and this gift is wonderful. You made my whole day.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.like.birthday=A birthday gift like this. You have good taste.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.neutral.birthday=Thanks. A simple gift on my birthday still means a lot.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_blacksmith.gift.dislike.birthday=It is my birthday and you brought that. Well. I still appreciate the thought.
